# Rebuild after finishing changes

When you finish implementing, editing, or fixing project code, run a production build before you stop. Do not leave source-only changes that the loaded Chrome extension will not pick up.

- From the project root: `npm run build` (`wxt build`).
- Do this even for small UI or content-script edits.
- If the user still has the extension loaded unpacked, remind them to reload it in `chrome://extensions` when the build output changed.
- Skip the rebuild only when the work did not change build inputs (for example docs-only or Cursor rules).
